    "Adjust forecasts downward if sentiment turns negative (e.g., sentiment < 0.0) and price is trending upward.",
    "Apply mean reversion bias: if forecast is significantly above recent 5-day average, reduce by 5-15% for next period.",
    "Increase downward bias when sentiment is positive (e.g., sentiment > 0.5) and price is trending downward.",
    "Correct for lag: if true outcome is significantly below forecast, reduce forecast by 10-20% for next period if sentiment remains neutral.",
    "Avoid overreacting to short-term sentiment shifts — apply smoothing filter (e.g., 3-period moving average) to sentiment before adjusting forecasts."
